I'll examine the current state of the relevant files before making changes.Let me locate the sidebar, the submenu component, and all z-index usages to diagnose the stacking issue.Let me find where `MainMenu` is rendered and inspect the layout folder and global styles.Let me check the global stylesheet and where `Collapsible` is used before finalizing.I have everything I need. Here's my analysis and the two targeted fixes.

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
1. **Mobile user info collapsed by default** — In the mobile `WindowsMenu` sheet, the wallet/user info block (`UserInfoPanel`) must be collapsed by default and show only a compact "basic info" header (avatar, name, status, balance), expandable to the full panel. Reuse the existing `Collapsible` component.
2. **MainMenu submenus invisible (z-index)** — The `MainMenu` dropdown/submenus don't appear; this is a stacking-order problem.

**Root Cause of the z-index bug**
The global stylesheet forces every Reka-UI floating surface to a very low layer:

```css
/* src/assets/main.css */
div[data-reka-popper-content-wrapper] {
  z-index: 2 !important;
}
```

Reka teleports every menu / submenu / popover into a `div[data-reka-popper-content-wrapper]` at the end of `<body>`. That wrapper is `position: fixed`, so it creates its **own stacking context** — the content's own `z-index` is irrelevant; only the wrapper's matters. With the wrapper pinned at `z-index: 2`, all menus sit **below** the app chrome:
- App.vue mobile backdrop → `z-100`
- App.vue / DesktopSidebar mobile sidebar → `z-150`
- DesktopSidebar mobile aside/backdrop → `z-40` / `z-50`

So on mobile (and wherever the sidebar overlays), the `MainMenu` submenus render behind the backdrop/sidebar and look "missing".

> Note: the previous change added `div[data-reka-popper-content-wrapper] { z-index: 150 !important; }` inside `WindowsMenu.vue`'s **scoped** `<style>`. Scoped styles compile to `…[data-v-xxxx]`, and that wrapper is created internally by Reka (it never carries WindowsMenu's scope id), so the rule never matched. It's dead code and is removed here.

**Fix:** raise the single global rule so menus float **above** the chrome (higher than `z-150`).

**Strategic Approach**
- `main.css`: bump the popper-wrapper `z-index` from `2` → `200` (above everything the app uses; app max is `z-150`).
- `WindowsMenu.vue`: on mobile, wrap `UserInfoPanel` in `<Collapsible :default-open="false">`, using `#icon` (avatar), `#title` (name) and `#summary` (status + wallet balance); desktop unchanged. Add the small computed getters needed for the collapsed summary. Remove the ineffective scoped popper rule.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- The global `z-index` bump affects **all** Reka surfaces (menus, submenus, tooltips, comboboxes). That is the desired behaviour; the app currently tops out at `z-150`, so `200` is safe. Menus will also correctly render above modals (`Modal.vue` = `z-50`), which is the expected UX for dropdowns.
- Desktop `WindowsMenu` layout is untouched (Collapsible is only rendered when `isMobile`).
- `Collapsible` is used exactly as-is (no changes to the shared component).

**Target Files**
- `src/assets/main.css` (modify — 1 declaration)
- `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` (modify)

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

1. **`src/assets/main.css`** — set the Reka popper wrapper to `z-index: 200` with an explanatory comment.
2. **`src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue`** — mobile branch uses `<Collapsible>` for the user info; add `user`/`userInitial`/`walletBalance`/`connected` computeds; import `Collapsible`; drop the dead scoped popper rule.

