### Design & UX notes (Designer lens)
- **Mobile collapsed state (default):** avatar (`#icon`) + name (`#title`) + a status pill and a wallet-balance pill (`#summary`) — the "basic info" glance. Expanding reveals the full `UserInfoPanel` (metrics, transactions, actions).
- **Tokens used:** `badge`-style pills built with `rounded-full`, `bg-base-100/60` and semantic `bg-success/15 text-success`; status uses `bg-success`/`bg-error` (colour **plus** text label, never colour alone).
- **Desktop untouched:** the fixed `w-[640px]` two-column panel and left `w-56` user column are identical to before.
- **Z-index:** `200` is deliberately the highest layer in the app (chrome tops out at `z-150`), so transient menus always win over persistent surfaces — consistent with existing `z-[150]` dropdown usages (e.g. `UserSelector`, `ProjectIconSelector`).

### Accessibility checklist
- Status is conveyed by **text** (`online`/`offline`) as well as colour.
- Wallet balance uses a formatted, monospaced value with a `wallet` icon.
- The balance pill is hidden when no balance is available (`v-if="walletBalance != null"`) to avoid empty/ambiguous state.
- No focus indicators removed; `Collapsible` retains its own affordance.

